      "name": "Why This Happens",
      "char_file": "발저림_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "The CDC estimates",
        "7 million US adults",
        "live with diabetic",
        "peripheral neuropathy",
        "",
        "High blood sugar damages nerves",
        "and the tiny vessels",
        "that feed them",
        "",
        "Two things speed this up,",
        "and one more turns it dangerous"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cause 1: Poor Blood Sugar Control",
      "char_file": "혈당계_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "The longer you've had diabetes",
        "and the higher your average",
        "blood sugar has run,",
        "",
        "the higher your risk",
        "of nerve damage climbs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Keep Blood Sugar in Range",
      "char_file": "운동화_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Keeping blood sugar",
        "in your target range",
        "is the main way to slow it",
        "",
        "Regular meals, prescribed",
        "medication, and walking",
        "all help"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cause 2: High Blood Pressure and Heart Disease",
      "char_file": "혈압계_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Research on people with diabetes",
        "links hypertension and",
        "cardiovascular disease",
        "",
        "to a higher risk of nerve damage,",
        "on top of blood sugar alone"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Manage Blood Pressure and Cholesterol Too",
      "char_file": "혈압계_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Don't just watch glucose -",
        "manage blood pressure",
        "and cholesterol alongside it",
        "",
        "Treating all three together",
        "protects your nerves better"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "The Real Danger: Missing a Foot Injury",
      "char_file": "발저림_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Once you can't feel your feet,",
        "small cuts and blisters",
        "go unnoticed",
        "",
        "Up to a third of people",
        "with diabetes develop",
        "a foot ulcer",
        "",
        "Amputation risk is about 11%",
        "from nerve damage alone,",
        "but jumps to 29% if blood flow",
        "to the foot is also poor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Check Your Feet Every Day",
      "char_file": "발저림_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Look over your feet",
        "every single day",
        "for cuts, blisters, or redness",
        "",
